 1→//! Bivvy - Interactive development environment setup automation.
 2→//!
 3→//! Bivvy is a CLI tool that replaces ad-hoc `bin/setup` scripts with
 4→//! declarative YAML configuration and a polished interactive CLI experience.
 5→//!
 6→//! # Modules
 7→//!
 8→//! - [`cli`] - Command-line interface and argument parsing
 9→//! - [`config`] - Configuration loading, parsing, and validation
10→//! - [`environment`] - Environment detection and resolution
11→//! - [`error`] - Error types and result aliases
12→//! - [`lint`] - Configuration validation and linting
13→//! - [`registry`] - Template registry and resolution
14→//! - [`runner`] - Step execution orchestration and dependency management
15→//! - [`shell`] - Shell command execution
16→//! - [`state`] - State management for execution history and preferences
17→//! - [`secrets`] - Secret detection and output masking
18→//! - [`steps`] - Step resolution and execution
19→//! - [`ui`] - Interactive prompts, spinners, and terminal output
20→//!
21→//! # Example
22→//!
23→//! ```
24→//! use bivvy::config::{InterpolationContext, resolve_string};
25→//!
26→//! // Resolve variables in a command
27→//! let mut ctx = InterpolationContext::new();
28→//! ctx.prompts.insert("mode".to_string(), "development".to_string());
29→//! let command = resolve_string("rails s -e ${mode}", &ctx).unwrap();
30→//! assert_eq!(command, "rails s -e development");
31→//! ```
32→//!
33→//! For file-based config loading, see the integration tests.
34→
